r" points to know here: \n\nThere is no "park" there. It\'s mostly GMO cow corn and soybean fields that use thousands of tons of carcinogenic Roundup that then ends up in the local water table.\n\nThe "environmental activists" mentioned are generally tied to a few shell corporations that have been renting the lands at basically zero rent while also not paying taxes. The "activists" are tied and have access to the woke Pickering city council, which has some of the most corrupt municipal city councilors in the country, e.g. Maurice Brenner, and Jenn O\'Connell, a wildly unpopular and incompetent MP who is on her way out of the door.\n\nThe cancellation of this project illustrates how ecoradicalism, gatekeeping, and red tape have essentially been deindustrializing Canada for several decades. Canada\'s infrastructure is worse than some third-world countries now. Nothing can be built in Canada.\n\nAll world-class cities like NY, Chicago, LA, Tokyo, and London have more than one major airport, not just for capacity issues, but for logistical reasons. Toronto opts instead to have more cow-corn fields instead.\n\nBeing near a nuclear power plant that has now been extended, this unique land assembly 25 minutes from downtown Toronto could have been a massive business opportunity for AI data centers. Private companies in the US are now investing $500 billion into building power-hungry massive data centers for AI infrastructure. None are going to be built in Canada thanks to such environmental fanaticism. A logistical airport and the nuclear plant would have made this place a massive attraction for private investment. These things have to be near cities to attract top talent. Cow-corn fields can be anywhere; they don\'t need to be 25 minutes from downtown Toronto.\n\nDespite the gaslighting by the "activists", Canadians won\'t go hungry because of 10,000 acres for economic development, in a country which STAT Canada says already has 165 million acres of farmland - the highest per capita globally. People are going hungry in Canada because of poverty and job loss, not because of a lack of farmland.', 'entity_set': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': [{'id_str': '287917452', 'name': 'Kevin Ashe', 'screen_name': 'kevinashe1', 'indices': [0, 11]}, {'id_str': '459359865', 'name': 'City of Pickering', 'screen_name': 'CityofPickering', 'indices': [12, 28]}, {'id_str': '269812167', 'name': 'Region of Durham', 'screen_name': 'RegionofDurham', 'indices': [29, 44]}, {'id_str': '770323159086206976', 'name': 'Peter Bethlenfalvy', 'screen_name': 'PBethlenfalvy', 'indices': [45, 59]}, {'id_str': '124190867', 'name': 'Transport Canada', 'screen_name': 'Transport_gc', 'indices': [60, 73]}, {'id_str': '409687240', 'name': 'Dr. Leslyn Lewis', 'screen_name': 'LeslynLewis', 'indices': [74, 86]}]}, 'richtext': {'richtext_tags': []}, 'media': {'inline_media': []}}}}, 'legacy': {'bookmark_count': 0, 'bookmarked': False, 'created_at': 'Mon Jan 27 17:42:43 +0000 2025', 'conversation_id_str': '1883915482610160017', 'display_text_range': [15, 294], 'entities': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'timestamps': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': [{'id_str': '24700876', 'name': 'Toronto Sun', 'screen_name': 'TheTorontoSun', 'indices': [0, 14]}, {'id_str': '287917452', 'name': 'Kevin Ashe', 'screen_name': 'kevinashe1', 'indices': [15, 26]}, {'id_str': '459359865', 'name': 'City of Pickering', 'screen_name': 'CityofPickering', 'indices': [27, 43]}, {'id_str': '269812167', 'name': 'Region of Durham', 'screen_name': 'RegionofDurham', 'indices': [44, 59]}, {'id_str': '770323159086206976', 'name': 'Peter Bethlenfalvy', 'screen_name': 'PBethlenfalvy', 'indices': [60, 74]}, {'id_str': '124190867', 'name': 'Transport Canada', 'screen_name': 'Transport_gc', 'indices': [75, 88]}, {'id_str': '409687240', 'name': 'Dr. Leslyn Lewis', 'screen_name': 'LeslynLewis', 'indices': [89, 101]}]}, 'favorite_count': 0, 'favorited': False, 'full_text': '@TheTorontoSun @kevinas